      "text": "We have the equation:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(x-3)^2 + (y+4)^2} + \\sqrt{(x+5)^2 + (y-8)^2} = 20\n\\]\n\nThis is the sum of distances from a point \\((x,y)\\) to two fixed points:\n\n- \\(F_1 = (3, -4)\\)\n- \\(F_2 = (-5, 8)\\)\n\nThe sum of distances is constant \\(20\\), so this is an ellipse with foci at \\(F_1\\) and \\(F_2\\).\n\nThe distance between the foci is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{(-5 - 3)^2 + (8 - (-4))^2}\n= \\sqrt{(-8)^2 + (12)^2}\n= \\sqrt{64 + 144}\n= \\sqrt{208}\n= 4\\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nThe answer is \\(4\\sqrt{13}\\).",
